menu "SPI AT master (external 8711 Wi-Fi)"

config WIFI_8711
	bool "External 8711 Wi-Fi chip over SPI"
	select SPI_AT_MASTER
	default n
	help
	  "An external 8711FA Wi-Fi companion exists."  Role-agnostic on
	  purpose: this is the symbol every Wi-Fi caller in app/protocol
	  (port_softap, port_tcp, jpgs_ingress, ebfs_ingress, cmd_debug) is
	  guarded on, so it is what "pause the Wi-Fi features" turns off --
	  each of those files has a working #else stub.

	  It selects SPI_AT_MASTER, which is the transport: WE drive SCLK and
	  CS and the 8711 runs Realtek's standard AT command set.  Turned on by
	  the wifi snippet, which also supplies the devicetree nodes that
	  transport binds to -- enabling the symbol on its own will not build.

	  DECLARED HERE, ALONGSIDE THE TRANSPORT IT SELECTS, because the module
	  it used to live in is gone.  It was app/wifi_8711/Kconfig's, back when
	  this symbol MEANT that module -- the SPI slave stack talking to an
	  8711 running custom in-house AT firmware.  The slave role was retired
	  in favour of the master role (10 MHz vs 25, and a vendor-supported
	  command set instead of one we maintained), the module was deleted, and
	  the symbol outlived it because "an 8711 exists" is a fact about the
	  BOARD rather than about which transport implements it.  Keeping the
	  name is what spares every #if in app/protocol from churning.

config SPI_AT_MASTER
	bool "AT-over-SPI toward the 8711, WE are the master"
	select SPI
	select SPI_RTL87X3G_DMA
	select DMA
	select GPIO
	default n
	help
	  The transport for the reversed-role SPI link: we drive SCLK and CS
	  at 25 MHz, the 8711 is the slave, and the two sync lines swap direction
	  (P4_1 becomes our input, P2_7 our output).  Frames are 16 KiB slots
	  carrying an 'A','T',len16 header, matching the vendor reference
	  example/atcmd_host/atcmd_host_spi.  Above it sit at_parser, at_client
	  and then at_wifi / at_socket, which is what app/protocol talks to.

	  Turned on by the wifi snippet, which also supplies the spi1_hs /
	  spi_at_master_resources / spi_at_master_device / psram1_nc devicetree
	  nodes this module binds to.  Enabling the symbol alone will not
	  build -- the DT nodes must come with it.

	  Selected by WIFI_8711 above, which is the role-agnostic "an external
	  8711 exists" switch that app/protocol's guards test.  It used to be
	  `depends on !WIFI_8711` instead, because that symbol then meant the
	  SLAVE stack and both claim P4_2..P4_5 -- the slave role has since been
	  retired and deleted, so the two are one arrangement rather than two
	  and there is no mutual exclusion left to express.

config SPI_AT_MASTER_SHELL
	bool "atm shell command group"
	depends on SPI_AT_MASTER && SHELL
	default y
	help
	  Register the `atm` shell commands: forward a typed AT command line to
	  the 8711 over SPI, hexdump both directions, and read back the sync
	  line levels and counters.  Defaults on because it is the only way to
	  drive the link by hand -- it was the harness's whole user interface
	  once, and it is still how you separate "the 8711 is not answering"
	  from "app/protocol never asked it anything".

endmenu
